[]($section)
## cool projects

- [wiretooth](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/wiretooth): a bluetooth transport proxy
  for wireguard.
- [lumine](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lumine): an x86_64/aarch64 UEFI bootloader
  that works, written in zig
- [envidiyuh](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/envidiyuh): a fast runtime for
  (byte-level) [markov chains](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markov_chain)
- [lexyc](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lexyc/): x86(64) compiler for a
  turing-complete esoteric programming language in zig
  ([see original](https://git.gay/noraaoki/xy))
- [brainfucc](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/brainfucc/): a optimizing brainfuck
  compiler targeting targeting native assembly, on x86_64 and riscv64

### miscellaneous projects

- [lain](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lain): a tiny and fast http/1.1 server library
  written in zig.
- [minimux](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/minimux): a tiny linux kernel + userspace
  experiment, primarily made to test lumine.
- [ziggymirror](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/ziggymirror/): a
  [community mirror](https://ziglang.org/news/announcing-community-mirrors/)
  for downloading zig written in posix shell
- [gopresence](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/gopresence/): discord presence
  library for golang programs (cross platform, and doesnt suck)
- [clispy](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/clispy/): a tiny lisp-like language.

### projects i contributed to

- [is-a.dev](https://github.com/is-a-dev/register/)

## interests

eh its more like i randomly start doing stuff but generally most of my likings
can be classified into:

